IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Crimes (Hostages) Act 1989 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND THE TOP-LEVEL
-- GOAL. Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03774.txt (compilation No.
-- 6, 10 March 2016). The accused asks: "Is what I did hostage-taking under the
-- Act; can I be charged in Australia; can I be convicted given a foreign
-- conviction; what must happen before trial; by when must I reappear after a
-- change of venue?"

§ `Nouns`

-- s 8(3).
DECLARE `Place of the act` IS ONE OF
    `in Australia`
    `on an Australian ship or aircraft`
    `elsewhere outside Australia`

DECLARE `Hostage case` HAS
    -- s 7
    `I seized or detained another person`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `I threatened to kill, injure or keep detaining them`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `I intended to compel an institution, organisation or person to act or abstain as a condition of release` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 8(1): the Convention in force for Australia (s 13 certificate)
    `the act was on`                                                IS A DATE
    `the Convention entered into force for Australia on`            IS A DATE
    -- s 8(3)
    `the place of the act`                                          IS A `Place of the act`
    `I was an Australian citizen at the time`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am present in Australia`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the aim was to compel an Australian legislative, executive or judicial institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 9(1), Article 12
    `the Geneva Conventions apply to it in an armed conflict`       IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 9(2)-(3): a single State
    `the act, I and the hostage are all of one State, where I now am other than by extradition` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 6(2)
    `I have been convicted abroad for the same conduct`             IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 10(1)
    `the Attorney-General has consented in writing`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 12(1)
    `a change of venue order was made on`                           IS A MAYBE DATE

DECLARE `Hostage position` HAS
    `hostage-taking (s 7)`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `an offence (s 8)`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `I may be imprisoned for life`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `chargeable (ss 8(3), 9)`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `convictable (s 6(2))`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `committable for trial (s 10)`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the latest day to reappear after a change of venue`            IS A MAYBE DATE

§ `Rules`

@ref s 7
GIVEN c IS A `Hostage case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is hostage-taking` c IF
        c's `I seized or detained another person`
    AND c's `I threatened to kill, injure or keep detaining them`
    AND c's `I intended to compel an institution, organisation or person to act or abstain as a condition of release`

-- s 8(1): after the Convention enters into force for Australia, which it is
-- from the start of that day (changed after the independent pass); (2): life.
@ref s 8(1)-(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Hostage case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an offence` c IF
        `it is hostage-taking` c
    AND c's `the act was on` AT LEAST c's `the Convention entered into force for Australia on`

-- s 8(3): in Australia, on an Australian ship or aircraft, or abroad by a
-- citizen, by someone now in Australia, or to compel an Australian
-- institution. s 9(1)-(3): not where Article 12 excludes the Convention, nor in
-- the single-State case.
@ref ss 8(3), 9
GIVEN c IS A `Hostage case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I may be charged` c IF
        `it is an offence` c
    AND `the place limb is met` c
    AND NOT (c's `the Geneva Conventions apply to it in an armed conflict`)
    AND NOT (c's `the act, I and the hostage are all of one State, where I now am other than by extradition`)

GIVEN c IS A `Hostage case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the place limb is met` c IF
        NOT (c's `the place of the act` EQUALS `elsewhere outside Australia`)
    OR  c's `I was an Australian citizen at the time`
    OR  c's `I am present in Australia`
    OR  c's `the aim was to compel an Australian legislative, executive or judicial institution`

-- s 6(2): not after a conviction abroad for the same conduct.
@ref s 6(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Hostage case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I may be convicted` c IF
        `I may be charged` c
    AND NOT (c's `I have been convicted abroad for the same conduct`)

-- s 10(1)-(2): committal needs the Attorney-General's written consent.
@ref s 10
GIVEN c IS A `Hostage case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I may be committed for trial` c IF
        `I may be charged` c
    AND c's `the Attorney-General has consented in writing`

-- s 12(1): "not later than 28 days after the day on which the order is made".
@ref s 12(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Hostage case`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the reappearance day for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `a change of venue order was made on`
    WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (d PLUS 28)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@ref ss 6-10, 12
@export default The position of a person accused of hostage-taking under the Crimes (Hostages) Act 1989 (Cth): whether the act is hostage-taking (seizing or detaining someone and threatening to kill, injure or keep detaining them, to compel an institution, organisation or person as a condition of release: s 7); whether it is an offence (after the Convention entered into force for Australia; life imprisonment: s 8); whether they may be charged in Australia (in Australia, on an Australian ship or aircraft, or abroad as a citizen, while present here, or to compel an Australian institution; not under Article 12 or in the single-State case: ss 8(3), 9); whether they may be convicted despite a foreign conviction (s 6(2)); whether they may be committed for trial (with the Attorney-General's consent: s 10); and the latest day to reappear after a change of venue (28 days after the order: s 12). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Hostage case`  @desc What I did and meant, the day, where, my citizenship and presence, the exclusions, any foreign conviction, the consent, and any change of venue
GIVETH A `Hostage position`
`the hostage position for` c MEANS
    `Hostage position` OF `it is hostage-taking` c, `it is an offence` c, `it is an offence` c, `I may be charged` c,
                          `I may be convicted` c, `I may be committed for trial` c, `the reappearance day for` c
